+# Jarvis | AuthorAi — baseline audit
+
+Audit date: 2026-09-30  
+Upstream: `a-ghorbani/pocketpal-ai`  
+Baseline commit: `4ebab32771df7d9e2554cd88a376bbda7d833da1`  
+PocketPal version: `1.18.0`  
+Jarvis version: `0.1.0` (`versionCode 1`)
+
+## Result
+
+PocketPal is a suitable base. It already contains a mature local/remote model layer, a bounded agent loop, extensible talents, web search, URL reading, model downloads, Pals, benchmarks, multimodal input, speculative decoding and four TTS engines. Jarvis keeps those capabilities and adds Android-specific tools in isolated `src/agent`, `src/voice`, and native `top.authorche.agent` modules.
+
+The Android application ID is `top.authorche.agent`. The React Native component is `JarvisAuthorAi`. The internal upstream Kotlin namespace remains `com.pocketpal` during the first phase to reduce merge risk; it is not the installed package ID.
+
+## Architecture found
+
+- React Native `0.82.1`, React `19.1.1`, TypeScript and MobX.
+- `src/store/ModelStore.ts`: local GGUF lifecycle, `llama.rn`, projection models, remote OpenAI-compatible servers, memory checks, hardware configuration and speculative decoding.
+- `src/store/ChatSessionStore.ts`: chats, prompt assembly, completion and persisted assistant/tool turns.
+- `src/services/agent/AgentRunner.ts`: bounded tool-call loop with cancellation, turn limits and normalized tool outcomes.
+- `src/services/talents`: registry and seven built-in talents: `web_search`, `read_url`, `calculate`, `datetime`, `render_html`, `device_status`, and `device_action`.
+- `src/services/search`: Brave, Tavily, Exa, Parallel and generic HTTP provider integrations using user-supplied keys.
+- `src/services/tts`: System, Kitten, Kokoro and Supertonic engines with streaming playback support.
+- `src/database`: WatermelonDB persistence for sessions, messages, global settings, local Pals and sync data.
+- `src/services/downloads` plus `android/.../download`: resumable/background model download infrastructure.
+- `src/screens/OnboardingScreens`: six-stage first-run flow and model selection.
+- `src/components/RemoteModelSheet`: OpenAI-compatible endpoint URL, model and API-key configuration.
+
+## llama.rn capability baseline
+
+Pinned version: `0.13.0-rc.5`.
+
+The current code actively uses Jinja chat templates, OpenAI-style tool definitions/tool calls and grammar triggers. It contains production paths for multimodal projection models and speculative draft models. The exact GPU/OpenCL performance on Mali-G720 and all runtime capabilities must be confirmed on the Xiaomi 14T Pro; availability in source is not treated as a successful device result.
+
+## Privacy and network inventory
+
+Local chat stays on-device when a local model is selected. Data can leave the phone only through features the user deliberately configures or invokes:
+
+- OpenAI-compatible remote model endpoints;
+- Hugging Face model discovery and downloads;
+- selected web-search provider and optional `r.jina.ai` page reader;
+- PalsHub/Supabase marketplace and authentication;
+- user-confirmed benchmark/feedback submission protected by Firebase App Check.
+
+Jarvis removes the feedback form from the About screen and will keep network actions visibly opt-in. PalsHub code is retained during baseline compatibility work but is not part of the Jarvis agent architecture; purchase/auth removal is a dedicated migration because deleting it blindly would break Pals persistence and tests.
+
+## Branding and signing completed
+
+- Display name: `Jarvis | AuthorAi`.
+- Application ID: `top.authorche.agent`.
+- Dark/mint visual accent.
+- Default built-in persona: Jarvis, Ukrainian by default with language mirroring and explicit action-safety rules.
+- Original MIT license and PocketPal copyright preserved.
+- One 4096-bit RSA release key is committed by the owner's explicit decision and used for all release builds.
+- Release certificate SHA-256: `30:49:19:5E:63:8C:8A:C9:B2:C4:1B:E1:98:1B:89:5C:09:D6:E4:82:D4:DC:03:FA:6B:B4:1A:59:F1:B1:6E:FD`.
+
+## Risks and decisions
+
+1. A public signing key lets anyone sign an APK with the same certificate. This is intentional for this repository, but it cannot establish publisher authenticity.
+2. The upstream release workflow is tightly coupled to PocketPal infrastructure, Firebase and iOS. Jarvis uses a separate Android-only workflow.
+3. FUTO Keyboard/FUTO Voice Input are reference implementations, not MIT dependencies. Their code and binaries must not be copied into this MIT fork without separate permission and license review.
+4. Android system control is permission-bound. Public APIs are preferred; Accessibility, Shizuku and Termux are explicit user-enabled capability tiers.
+5. Physical-device metrics (cold start, tok/s, RTF, RAM, temperature and battery) cannot be honestly produced in CI. The test protocol is documented and must be run on the Xiaomi 14T Pro before marking performance criteria complete.
+
+## Acceptance status
+
+- Source audit: complete.
+- Rebrand and signing configuration: complete.
+- TypeScript, localization, ESLint and unit checks: complete.
+- Linux Android release build: delegated to the committed GitHub Actions workflow because this workspace has no Android SDK/NDK.
+- Physical Xiaomi 14T Pro baseline: pending device run; no numbers are fabricated.
