+# Voice research gate
+
+This document defines the measurements required before selecting the default Jarvis STT engine. It intentionally contains no invented Xiaomi results.
+
+## Candidates
+
+| Candidate                  | Intended use                              | uk/en/de                            | Android integration                                                | License gate                        |
+| -------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |
+| whisper.cpp / `whisper.rn` | Built-in dictation and Live Voice         | Multilingual; measure each language | React Native or isolated JNI module                                | Verify binding and model licenses   |
+| sherpa-onnx                | Streaming STT, VAD and possible Piper TTS | Model-dependent                     | JNI/ONNX Runtime                                                   | Verify every model                  |
+| FUTO Voice Input           | Optional external short dictation         | Model-dependent; measure            | `ACTION_RECOGNIZE_SPEECH` only when supported by installed release | FUTO Source First; do not copy code |
+| Vosk                       | Small command fallback                    | Model-dependent                     | JNI/Android SDK                                                    | Verify model license                |
+| Android SpeechRecognizer   | Last-resort system provider               | Device/provider-dependent           | Platform API                                                       | May use network; disclose provider  |
+
+FUTO `SpeechRecognizer`/`RecognitionService` support is not assumed. Jarvis probes actual intent/service availability at runtime. Live Voice never depends on an installed keyboard because external activities do not provide the PCM/VAD/partial-result/barge-in control needed by a continuous session.
+
+## Xiaomi 14T Pro protocol
+
+Record 50 utterances per language (Ukrainian, English, German), including short commands, contact names, mixed Ukrainian/English technical speech and 30–60 second dictation. For each candidate capture:
+
+- WER per language and command intent accuracy;
+- median and p95 first partial-result latency;
+- real-time factor for 5 s, 15 s and 60 s audio;
+- peak RSS and model-load time;
+- battery delta and thermal status over a 10-minute session;
+- behavior with speaker, wired headset and Bluetooth headset;
+- interruption latency when barge-in stops TTS.
+
+Use fixed 16 kHz mono PCM recordings for comparable accuracy tests, then repeat live microphone tests with WebRTC/Android noise suppression. Results are valid only when the exact model filename, checksum, thread count and backend are recorded.
+
+## Provisional architecture
+
+`AudioRecord → AEC/NS → VAD → built-in streaming STT → agent loop → sentence queue → TTS`
+
+The external FUTO path is a separate short-dictation convenience. The default engine is selected only after real measurements on the target phone.
+
+## Implemented short-dictation bridge
+
+Jarvis now exposes a microphone button in the chat composer and launches the standard Android `RecognizerIntent.ACTION_RECOGNIZE_SPEECH` chooser with `EXTRA_PREFER_OFFLINE`. The returned text is inserted into the current draft; cancellation returns without changing the draft, and missing providers or empty/error results are surfaced to the user.
+
+This is provider-neutral. It deliberately does not identify the selected app as FUTO or promise offline processing: Android treats `EXTRA_PREFER_OFFLINE` as a preference, and only an on-device test of the installed provider can establish actual behavior. FUTO compatibility remains unverified until tested against the stable FUTO Voice Input build on the Xiaomi 14T Pro.
